Z||000020||The Fieromaster||12-19-2001||09:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Two88GTs:<BR><B> Can you get me an office chair "base" that tilts/swivels with wheels plus a gas-charged height adjuster?  How much with shipping?  Come now, the amateur chair builders in the Forum wants to know.  I have a mint seat with speakers that I pulled from a yard car just for this purpose.  TIA!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Dont forget a wide enough base so when you DO lean back you dont bust your dome on the ground cause the chair fell over!!<P><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">    <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000021||86seyellow||12-19-2001||09:49 AM||||a 5 prong base with gas lift and tilt/swivel should cost around 45.00 OR LESS. ill check price today for you. Also you will probably have to make a base that out of 3/4 ply to mount the chair to. After you get the base you should drill the holes where needed then use T inserts that will enable u to attach the base<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||deceler8||12-19-2001||11:22 AM||||No, it's an IBM 300XL on the desk.<P>As for leaning all the way back, I can tilt the seat all the way back and it doesn't fall over.<P>I wish I had done this earlier. It looks great and it's damn comfortable. The base I used I found on trash pickup day and I had to weld it in the upright position as it was broken. But that doesn't matter as the seat reclines anyway.<P>Just about everything in my office is homemade...the desk is made out of oak boards on a PVC pipe base with sewing machine drawers for storage.<P>Hey Archie...post some photos of the leather "Fiero office chairs" when you get them done.<P>If you want to get off cheap, you could try your local Goodwill or an office supply store for a broken or cheap office chair base.||||reg||1
